== Effects ==
* Spawns 6 {{e|Troll Bomb}}s, generally near the center of the [[room]].

== Notes ==
* This card's active effect is identical to {{i|Anarchist Cookbook}}'s.
* Although visually unchanged, all passive {{e|Bomb}} effect items affect the spawned Troll Bombs unless otherwise noted.
* The bombs spawn one after the other, meaning that they will also explode one after the other and can push each other around.
** If the room is exited before all bombs are spawned, the remaining bombs will not continue to spawn upon re-entering the room.
* Exiting the room will reset the troll bombs' fuses.

== Strategy ==
* By repeatedly exiting and re-entering the room, the bombs can be slowly pushed towards a [[tinted rock]] or a {{r|Secret Room}}'s entrance.

== Synergies ==
* {{I|Tarot Cloth}}: Spawns '''13''' troll bombs.
** {{I|Tarot Cloth|r}} + {{i|Blank Card}}: Only spawns 6 troll bombs if used with blank card.
* {{t|Blasting Cap}}: All troll bombs have a 10% chance to drop a {{e|Bomb}} pickup when it explodes.
* {{i|Remote Detonator}}: The Troll Bombs generated will not explode until Remote Detonator is activated.

== Interactions ==
* {{I|Bomber Boy}}: Not recommended. The cross pattern explosion makes it very hard to avoid taking damage.
* {{i|Mr. Mega}}: No effect.
* {{I|Pyromaniac}}: Spawned bombs can be used for mass healing.
* {{T|Safety Scissors}}: Spawned troll bombs become bomb pickups.
* {{i|Scatter Bombs|a+}}: Not recommended. Each Troll Bomb will spawn several smaller bombs upon exploding, making it very hard to avoid taking damage.
** {{dlc|r}} No visual change can be seen with the Troll Bombs, but the smaller bombs have the sprite of the smaller normal bombs.

